<node id="1183999" title="Re^5: How to add hyperlink for every table data using perl?" created="2017-03-09 02:19:57" updated="2017-03-09 02:19:57" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;what is the purpose of (.) you added in front of every line ?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That's the string concatenation operator, see [doc://perlop#Additive-Operators|perlop]. &lt;c&gt;'&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="' . $href_to_what{$word} . '"&gt;' . $word . '&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;'&lt;/c&gt; concatenates those five strings together into a single string. In this case it's the same as writing &lt;c&gt;"&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=\"$href_to_what{$word}\"&gt;$word&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;"&lt;/c&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
